stsh:NodeExpressionShape sh:or _:dc9edc1ea9f24db983457fe0241a3704 ;
	rdfs:comment "Accepts a constant (IRI/literal), sh:this, a blank node carrying a known sh:/shnex: node-expression defining predicate, a blank node structurally shaped like a SHACL Function call or a custom List Parameter Function call, or a call to a declared custom Named Parameter Expression Function. Deliberately shallow beyond that - see rdfs:comment on stsh:NodeExpressionFunctionCallShape and the section header above for the exact scope boundary."@en ;
	rdfs:label "Well-formed SHACL node expression"@en ;
	sh:targetClass sh:NodeExpression ;
	a sh:NodeShape .
stsh:SelectQueryTextShape sh:property _:a6a285f3901aa0fdcdea819fd38d64d6 .
_:a6a285f3901aa0fdcdea819fd38d64d6 sh:message "The text of sh:select must be a SELECT query (optional PREFIX and BASE lines, then SELECT)."@en ;
	sh:flags "is" ;
	sh:pattern "^\\s*((PREFIX\\s+[^\\s:]*:\\s*<[^>]*>|BASE\\s+<[^>]*>)\\s*)*SELECT\\b" ;
	sh:path sh:select .
stsh:SelectQueryTextShape sh:targetSubjectsOf sh:select ;
	rdfs:comment "SPARQL Extensions 3: the value of sh:select is a SELECT query. The text must be one: optional PREFIX and BASE lines, then SELECT. An empty string, or text that begins with anything else, is rejected here; the engine otherwise fails with a parse error only when the shapes are run (pySHACL parses it when the shape is loaded). SHACL cannot check the rest of the grammar, so a query that begins correctly but is malformed is still the engine's to report. Applies wherever sh:select is used: a SPARQL constraint, a SELECT validator, a SPARQL target, a node expression written in place."@en ;
	rdfs:label "Text of a sh:select is a SELECT query"@en ;
	a sh:NodeShape .
