	sh:path sh:ignoredProperties .
stsh:IgnoredPropertiesLanguageInMinListLengthShapes sh:targetSubjectsOf sh:languageIn , sh:ignoredProperties ;
	rdfs:comment "Mirrors the official SHACL 1.2 WG draft's own minListLength additions to shsh:ShapeShape for these two predicates - an empty sh:ignoredProperties or sh:languageIn list is rejected outright (Violation, unlike the Warning-level sh:in/sh:xone checks above, matching the official draft's own severity choice for these two - no explicit sh:severity override there either). Purely additive: pySHACL's own bundled base graph already correctly checks list-of-IRI/list-of-string membership for both, unmodified and untouched here - only the missing minimum-length check is added."@en ;
	rdfs:label "sh:ignoredProperties / sh:languageIn minimum list length"@en ;
	a sh:NodeShape .
stsh:InIsListShape sh:property _:d7731f7a4f725d0664e0227063e4a281 .
_:d7731f7a4f725d0664e0227063e4a281 sh:minListLength 0 ;
	sh:path sh:in .
stsh:InIsListShape sh:targetSubjectsOf sh:in ;
	rdfs:comment "The Working Group's shsh:ShapeShape only limits sh:in to one value, and its shsh:inSubjectsShape (minimum length 1, Warning) is the only place the value is checked as a list, so a single IRI is a warning at most. A value that is not a list is not an allowed-values list at all, so this is a Violation, and an empty list stays the warning above (sh:minListLength 0 asks for a well-formed list of any length)."@en ;
	rdfs:label "The value of sh:in is a list"@en ;
	a sh:NodeShape .
